  "_meta": {
    "version": "2.0.0",
    "updated": "2026-10-12",
    "description": "The roster of printers Kiln's G-code validator knows by name, plus the generic profile it holds any other machine to. Each named row carries display_name only. A printer's enforced limits (hotend, bed, chamber, feedrate, minimum Z, volumetric flow, build volume), its curated hardware variants and the notes behind them are served per printer from Kiln's catalogue when the printer is set up, and the loader parses them in under the row's id. A row with no limits is never a profile: a printer whose record this install does not hold is held to the generic 'default' row.",
    "default_row": "The floor. 'default' applies to a printer Kiln has not been told the model of, and to a catalogued printer whose record is not held here. Its hotend ceiling is the PTFE-safe 240 C, because whether a hotend is lined is part of the served record and an install without the record cannot know; its other limits sit below every catalogued printer's. It is enforced as a CRITICAL block rule by the G-code interceptor, as a ceiling, never a guard band.",
    "roster_contract": "Every id here is a row in printer_intelligence.json, slicer_profiles.json, design_knowledge/printer_profiles.json and design_knowledge/printer_material_compatibility.json, and has its record in Kiln's catalogue; adding a printer is a two-repo change. No roster row may carry a limit field -- tests/test_registry_mirror.py fails the file if one does, so a number cannot drift back in.",
    "local_overrides": "A person's own limits for a machine live in ~/.kiln/local_printer_overrides.json and may only tighten a served record. A limit above the generic floor for a printer with no record stands only once a person has confirmed it."
  },
